>>Is there a way to collect water from a sink/fountain/moat/swamp?  I've
>>got lots of lawful alters at which to make Holy Water, but no water in
>>which to do so.
>
>	Sorry, but the only way to get additional water other than finding it
>is to collect some other potions that you don't need, then #dip them into a
>fountain twice.  The first time you dip a potion it'll become diluted, then
>the second time it'll become water.

Aside from using wands of cancellation and unicorn horns, you can get
holy water by dipping potions in a POOL. This may seem like a small
distinction to dipping in fountains, but having water walking boots can
in fact be quite useful, since a pool never dries up, so you can make
(almost) unlimited numbers of potions of holy water and blank scrolls. 
Basically, it's the wand of cancellation you have when you don't have a
wand of cancellation.

